Third-party components
----------------------
AmberCell orchestrates and documents containers that may pull third-party
images and daemons. Those components retain their own licenses and copyrights.
Operators must review and comply with each upstream license before deployment.

Notable upstreams commonly referenced by this project (non-exhaustive):

  - Postfix / OpenSMTPD / Exim / Sendmail — respective MTA licenses
  - Dovecot / Cyrus / Courier — respective POP3/IMAP licenses
  - vsftpd / ProFTPD / Pure-FTPd — respective FTP server licenses
  - OpenSSH / Dropbear — respective SSH server licenses
  - Nginx / Apache httpd / Caddy / lighttpd — respective HTTP server licenses
  - BusyBox / inetutils telnetd — respective Telnet daemon licenses
  - Redis, Mosquitto, MariaDB/MySQL, PostgreSQL, Samba, MongoDB,
    Elasticsearch, Ollama — respective project licenses
  - Docker / containerd / runc / Compose — respective container runtime licenses

Image digests and SPDX identifiers for pinned builds will be recorded in
release SBOMs (CycloneDX or SPDX) when releases are published. This NOTICE is
a pointer only; it does not restate full third-party license texts.
